  "estimatedMinutes": 1,
  "statement": "Given the set of \\(n\\) numbers, \\(n\\gt1,\\) of which one is \\(1-\\dfrac1n\\) and all the others are \\(1.\\) The arithmetic mean of the \\(n\\) numbers is:",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "\\(1\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "\\(n-\\dfrac1n\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "\\(n-\\dfrac1{n^2}\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "\\(1-\\dfrac1{n^2}\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "\\(1-\\dfrac1n-\\dfrac1{n^2}\\)"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "d",
    "value": null
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1962-p8.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "The sum is \\[ (n-1)+\\left(1-\\frac1n\\right)=n-\\frac1n. \\] Dividing by \\(n\\) gives \\(1-\\frac{1}{n^2}.\\)\n\nThus, the correct answer is D.",
      "hints": [
        "There are \\(n-1\\) copies of \\(1\\)",
        "Add all \\(n\\) numbers, then divide the sum by \\(n\\)"
      ],
